issue.description:
ApplyRequestTransforms and ApplyResponseTransforms do not implement rename or default - they leave the source field in place and never error on a missing source. Production code in internal/server/adapter_executor.go, 4 failing tests / 8 subtests.

  rename simple field   got {"newName":"value","oldName":"value"} want {"newName":"value"}
  rename nested field   got {"data":{"newField":"value","oldField":"value"}} want {"data":{"newField":"value"}}
  rename missing field  got error <nil>, wantErr true
  default missing field got {} want {"newField":"defaultValue"}
  default nested field  got {"data":{}} want {"data":{"count":0}}
  response rename       got {"newField":"value","oldField":"value"} want {"newField":"value"}
  multiple transforms   got {"data":{"new":"value","old":"value"}} want {"data":{"added":42,"new":"value"}}
  ApplyResponseTransformsToReader got {"new":"value","old":"value"} want {"new":"value"}

So rename is currently COPY, not MOVE, and default is a no-op. For a proxy that rewrites request/response bodies this is a correctness hole: a rename that leaves the original behind leaks a field the operator believes was removed. Fix the implementation, not the expectations.

Evidence: .beads/green-evidence.md (bead seam-d33d0b9c).
